{
 "_doc": "[tunes] The song library (systems/tunes.gd). Files are audio/songs/<id>.mp3; a song whose file is missing is skipped everywhere (no CD, not on the CD player, not in the shuffle), so new MP3s can be dropped in by id later (then run an import). group: story or a planet id. kind: title / cinematic / villain (CD player only unless shuffle), playlist (background shuffle on its planet), night (only at night on its planet), restored (only once its planet is mostly restored). unlock: start (owned from the start) or cd (a CD found in the rubble on found_on). artist: an id in artists. Names, titles, genres, bios and descs are English and translated at display time (tr). artist home: the planet the artist lived on; every intact CD is found on its artist's home planet (found_on). scratched: rare one-play teaser CDs of songs you do not own yet, per_planet of them on each planet (planet/cd_finds.gd). State: GameState.flags.songs {found, pity, pending, scratched (held), scratch_left, scratch_cool, plays}.",
 "_doc_adding": "[v6sound] ADDING A SONG (no code): put the file (mp3, ogg or wav) in audio/songs/ or in a folder below it named after a planet (audio/songs/ochre/). That is enough: a file with no entry here is picked up with \"defaults\" (title from the file name, owned from the start, plays on its folder's planet, or everywhere from the main folder). Add an entry to \"songs\" to say more. The id is the file name in lower case with _ for spaces (My New Song.mp3 -> my_new_song), or give \"file\". Optional per song: \"planets\": [\"verdance\"] or [\"all\"] (where it plays; without it the group decides); \"moments\": any of title, intro, explore, night, restored, base_restored, launch, ending (when it plays; without it the kind decides); \"weight\": how often (1 = normal, 2 = twice as often, 0 = never in the shuffle); \"volume_db\": trim in dB (-3 = a bit quieter); \"unlock\": start (owned at once) or cd (found as a CD on found_on). Check with: python3 tools/check_songs.py. See docs/ADJUSTING.md.",
 "_doc_rules": "[v6sound] RULES: main_theme: the song that opens the title, is the most common and never plays twice in a row. song_db: level of all songs. restored_at: how restored (0..1) a planet must be for \"restored\" songs. \"planets\".<id> may override gap_s, first_gap_s, landing_gap_s, main_share, story_weight, other_planet_weight and restored_at for that planet, and \"songs\" there lists ids that play on it at full weight whatever their group.",
